      "title": "Part C: Medicare through a private plan",
      "narration": "Medicare Advantage, Part C, lets Dennis receive his Medicare benefits through a private plan that Medicare pays a fixed monthly amount per member. To join he must have Parts A and B and live in the plan’s service area. The plan must cover everything Original Medicare covers, except hospice, which Original Medicare continues to pay, and most plans include Part D drug coverage and extras such as dental, vision, hearing and fitness benefits. Dennis keeps paying his Part B premium, and the plan may charge its own premium, often zero. The plan’s rules, networks and cost sharing replace Medicare’s.",
